;;==== SWP|TX 023 - H6 Reproduction: Primality Gate · 02 · let / invocation ==== =========================
(print "--- [SWP|TX 023 - H6 Reproduction: Primality Gate · 02 · let / invocation] ---")
;;Audit ref: Audit/SWP/ROUND-01-FINDINGS.md #H6 — SWP|C>DEFINE-PRIMORDIAL-POOL bound <primality> but never
;;included it in the enforce fold; only 5 fully composable conditions (weighted, has-OURO, has-WKDA,
;;has-LKDA, exactly-3-tokens) actually gated designation. Owner: primality also means exempt from
;;low-liquidity gates / never autonomously disabled — the real guardrail here, silently unenforced.
;;
;;Attempted a live "lookalike pool" adversarial reproduction (same 3 tokens, different order, p=false)
;;and it's not constructible — confirmed something stronger than either of us assumed going in. Tried
;;issuing a same-token-set pool in a different order; hit "Pool already exists for given Tokens!" from
;;SWP::UEV_New/UEV_CheckAgainstMass (15_SWP.pact:1058-1122), which checks new token SETS against every
;;existing pool of the same category via pure containment (UEV_CheckAgainst uses `contains`, not
;;positional equality) — completely order-independent. Once the real OURO|WKDA|LKDA pool exists, no
;;second pool sharing that token set can EVER be issued, in any order, with any weights. This confirms
;;the owner's assessment directly: the only theoretical exposure window was a one-time bootstrap race
;;(front-running the very first OURO|WKDA|LKDA pool issuance, before the real one existed) — already
;;closed on mainnet since the real pool was issued correctly first. Live adversarial reproduction against
;;the *current*, populated state is structurally impossible, not just hard to construct.
(let
    (
        (ref-TS01-A:module{TalosStageOne_AdminV1} TS01-A)
        (ref-SWP:module{SwapperV3} SWP)
        (pool1:string "W|DLK-98c486052a51|OURO-98c486052a51|DWK-98c486052a51")
    )
    ;;Regression check: the real, primality=true primordial pool must still be (re-)designatable with the
    ;;new primality enforce in place.
    (ref-TS01-A::SWP|A_DefinePrimordialPool pool1)
    (print (format "H6 fix — real primordial pool re-designation still works: {}" [(ref-SWP::UR_PrimordialPool)]))
)
